WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.269 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:03.269 --> 00:00:06.473
-Welcome, everybody,
to "Corrections."

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.273
We're back.

00:00:07.273 --> 00:00:08.374
We took a week off.

00:00:08.374 --> 00:00:10.310
We did not do "Corrections"
last week.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.913
We, instead, did a
"Specjackular,
which was a celebration

00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:16.982
[ Laughter ]
of the first 50 episodes
of "Corrections."

00:00:16.982 --> 00:00:21.187
So, last week was not,
technically, a "Corrections."

00:00:21.187 --> 00:00:22.688
It was a "Specjackular."

00:00:22.688 --> 00:00:25.225
If you missed it,

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.226
it's available
to stream on Peacock.

00:00:28.327 --> 00:00:30.063
Although, I have been told,
by some people

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:34.534
inside the Peacock
infrastructure

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:39.205
that, if you go, it will be
a little buggy right now

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:41.107
because so many people
are logging on

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.310
[ Laughter ]
to watch the "Specjackular."

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:47.113
They weren't prepared
for the onslaught.

00:00:48.781 --> 00:00:51.084
It is -- not going to lie --
it's a little bit hard

00:00:51.084 --> 00:00:56.322
to do a regular "Corrections"
after a "Specjackular."

00:00:56.322 --> 00:00:59.192
[ Laughter ]
Bit of a hangover.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:01.060
[ Laughter ]
And, look, sometimes

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:04.163
a hangover is fun and sometimes

00:01:04.163 --> 00:01:06.266
it's "Hangover Part III."

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:08.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:11.303 --> 00:01:12.572
I --

00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.708
A beer koozie is a portmanteau

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:19.145
of beer and cozy.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.047
I said it was a portmanteau

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:23.816
of beer and koozie.

00:01:23.816 --> 00:01:25.085
That's obviously wrong.

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:30.323
You look down your nose
at something.

00:01:30.323 --> 00:01:33.826
You don't look down at your nose
at something,

00:01:33.826 --> 00:01:35.194
which is what I said,
and I was told,

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.097
if you do that, you're going
to get crossed eyes.

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.698
[ Laughter ]

00:01:39.698 --> 00:01:41.701
I talked

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:44.537
about Donald Trump thinking that

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.507
his favorite participant
in "The Hunger Games"

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:48.641
would be Joey Chestnut.

00:01:50.242 --> 00:01:51.411
Someone said something --

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:52.645
a jackal said something
I think is true --

00:01:52.645 --> 00:01:55.581
that Donald Trump would probably
call Joey Chestnut

00:01:55.581 --> 00:01:56.883
Joey Hot Dog.

00:01:56.883 --> 00:02:00.753
[ Laughter ]

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:01.754
And I think that's right.

00:02:03.223 --> 00:02:06.392
I think he would think
Joey Chestnut

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.362
was a guy who won
a chestnut eating contest.

00:02:09.362 --> 00:02:10.964
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.001 --> 00:02:17.904
Oh, you don't get tested
for rabies.

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:20.106
This is very important.

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:21.640
You do not get tested
for rabies.

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:24.977
If you get bitten,
you get a rabies shot,

00:02:24.977 --> 00:02:27.080
out of an abundance of caution.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.315
There's no test for rabies.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.418
But if you leave a comment
under a YouTube video,

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:33.853
that's how you know you have it.

00:02:33.853 --> 00:02:36.122
[ Laughter ]

00:02:37.756 --> 00:02:39.993
The only way to test
for rabies is

00:02:39.993 --> 00:02:42.161
to cut off the head
and examine the brain.

00:02:42.161 --> 00:02:43.930
[ Laughter ]

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:46.499
So, if you ever see
like a white van

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:49.202
that has the words

00:02:49.202 --> 00:02:50.703
"Free rabies test" on it...

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.172
[ Laughter ]

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.641
...steer clear!

00:02:55.541 --> 00:02:56.242
Mm.

00:02:57.644 --> 00:02:59.012
So we had, um...

00:03:02.281 --> 00:03:04.283
...his picture of

00:03:04.283 --> 00:03:08.120 line:0%
crystal meth coming
in four different sizes.

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:09.121 line:0%
It was a punch line of a joke.

00:03:09.121 --> 00:03:11.157 line:0%
And one you said those are not

00:03:11.157 --> 00:03:14.961 line:0%
four different bags
of crystal meth.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:18.031 line:0%
That's the same bag scaled down.

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.566 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:21.734 line:0%
Which is true.

00:03:23.269 --> 00:03:27.206
Now, we had four different bags,

00:03:27.206 --> 00:03:29.074
but we left them out

00:03:29.074 --> 00:03:31.344
and they went missing!

00:03:31.344 --> 00:03:34.480
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.316
They went missing!

00:03:39.418 --> 00:03:43.056
And so then I put up a note
for the crew...

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:47.193
[ Laughter ]

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:50.763
...that said, "Put them back
where they were

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.932
and nobody's going
to get in trouble."

00:03:54.601 --> 00:03:56.402
And then the crew left a note
and said,

00:03:56.402 --> 00:03:58.604
"We forget what they look like."

00:03:58.604 --> 00:04:00.773
[ Laughter ]

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:04.510
So, I put out four more bags
and they went missing.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:07.647
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.083 --> 00:04:13.653
And I don't know who took it.

00:04:13.653 --> 00:04:14.954
But I do know...

00:04:17.790 --> 00:04:19.859
...that I went
to the cue card office...

00:04:19.859 --> 00:04:21.494
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.494 --> 00:04:24.097
...which is usually a mess,

00:04:24.097 --> 00:04:26.332
and it was super organized.

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:30.803
[ Laughter ]

00:04:30.803 --> 00:04:34.674
Someone had taken apart
all the Sharpies

00:04:34.674 --> 00:04:36.142
and put them back together.

00:04:36.142 --> 00:04:38.144
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.144 --> 00:04:40.613
Hey, this is a comment
for you guys.

00:04:40.613 --> 00:04:42.648
I don't know.
This is obviously --

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:46.652
You've spent time on YouTube,

00:04:46.652 --> 00:04:48.153
in the YouTube comments section.

00:04:48.153 --> 00:04:51.324
Sometimes one of you
will write first.

00:04:54.192 --> 00:04:56.796
But you're not first.

00:04:56.796 --> 00:04:59.665
It's shocking to me how often
this happens, because, again, I,

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.601
as we've established,
a core truth of "Corrections,"

00:05:02.601 --> 00:05:05.504
I'm the one who reads
all these comments

00:05:05.504 --> 00:05:06.872
and one of you will write,

00:05:06.872 --> 00:05:10.309
"First!" with an exclamation
point, but you're second.

00:05:10.309 --> 00:05:12.912
Someone else is first.

00:05:12.912 --> 00:05:15.581
And I think what happens is

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.216
you realize you're going
to be first

00:05:17.216 --> 00:05:19.918
and you celebrate
a little bit too long.

00:05:19.918 --> 00:05:21.253
I think you see it
and you're like,

00:05:21.253 --> 00:05:22.889
"Ooh hoo hoo hoo!

00:05:22.889 --> 00:05:24.023
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.023 --> 00:05:25.958
Look at this!
Look at me!"

00:05:25.958 --> 00:05:30.496
Bang, bang, bang, bang, bang.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.398
Bunk!
And you're [bleep] second.

00:05:32.398 --> 00:05:34.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:39.071 --> 00:05:42.041
We talked about how

00:05:42.041 --> 00:05:45.578
Brian Kilmeade
said the worst part

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:47.613
of Donald Trump's presidency was
the two months

00:05:47.613 --> 00:05:49.749
between the election
and the insurrection,

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:53.418
but the problem was we said
three months.

00:05:53.418 --> 00:05:56.322
And it was pointed out
it's actually only two months

00:05:56.322 --> 00:05:58.591
between the election
and the insurrection.

00:05:58.591 --> 00:06:01.727
Ian wrote that joke and I --
I know what he did.

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:04.896
He thought November, December,
January -- three months.

00:06:04.896 --> 00:06:06.298
I know what he didn't do,

00:06:06.298 --> 00:06:08.000
which was check his work.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:11.304
[ Laughter ]

00:06:13.572 --> 00:06:17.977
I said the plural of Batman
would be Batmen.

00:06:17.977 --> 00:06:20.012
It's Batsmen.

00:06:20.012 --> 00:06:22.414
[ Laughter ]

00:06:22.414 --> 00:06:25.550
We had -- man, oh, man,
did we have some --

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:29.856
We had some really nice cameos
in the "Specjackular."

00:06:29.856 --> 00:06:32.124
We had a lot of friends
of the show

00:06:32.124 --> 00:06:34.493
who, you know, we reached out,
they sent in videos.

00:06:34.493 --> 00:06:35.862
It was really fun to show you.

00:06:37.663 --> 00:06:39.432
While I was working
on this cameos,

00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:41.834
I realized, you know,
there's that app, Cameo,

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:45.738
where you can get celebrities
to make a video for you.

00:06:45.738 --> 00:06:48.040
And I'm not going to say who,

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:52.111
but there was a former mayor
who was on Cameo,

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:54.680
and I felt pretty confident
I could trick that mayor

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:57.416
into making a video
for the "Specjackular."

00:06:57.416 --> 00:06:59.485
What I would do is write
this former mayor --

00:06:59.485 --> 00:07:01.153
not going to say who --
and I would say,

00:07:01.153 --> 00:07:03.722
"Hey, former
Mayor [insert name there],

00:07:03.722 --> 00:07:07.593
man, those jackals in the press

00:07:07.593 --> 00:07:08.861
sure give you a hard time.

00:07:08.861 --> 00:07:11.297
I got a lot of jackals
giving me trouble at work.

00:07:11.297 --> 00:07:13.232
Would you record a video
saying your name

00:07:13.232 --> 00:07:16.135
and saying, "Don't let
the jackals get you down"?

00:07:16.135 --> 00:07:17.736
And I would trick
that former mayor

00:07:17.736 --> 00:07:20.739
into participating
in the "Specjackular."

00:07:20.739 --> 00:07:22.574
But, unfortunately,
that former mayor,

00:07:22.574 --> 00:07:23.910
I think he might be --

00:07:23.910 --> 00:07:25.077
and, again,
I'm not going to name names --

00:07:25.077 --> 00:07:26.646
I think he might be
in some legal trouble.

00:07:26.646 --> 00:07:28.447
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.447 --> 00:07:32.385
He's currently
not making Cameos.

00:07:32.385 --> 00:07:33.752
That was a lost opportunity.

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:35.221
And I know some of you
may be thinking, "Oh!

00:07:35.221 --> 00:07:37.490
I wish you hadn't said anything.

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.557
Now you won't be able to do it."

00:07:38.557 --> 00:07:40.893
Oh, I think I can still
trick him.

00:07:40.893 --> 00:07:42.161
[ Laughter ]
Or her.

00:07:47.866 --> 00:07:48.967
This is a coincidence.

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:51.003
This is not a segue
that was planned.

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.838
We had a joke
about Rudy Giuliani

00:07:52.838 --> 00:07:55.308
and I said that he...

00:07:55.308 --> 00:07:58.944
[ Laughter ]

00:07:58.944 --> 00:08:02.515
...he looked like an animal
in the reptile house,

00:08:02.515 --> 00:08:05.317
but then we showed a frog
and a bunch of you said,

00:08:05.317 --> 00:08:06.518
"That's an amphibian."

00:08:06.518 --> 00:08:09.388
Sal would like you
to know he knew that,

00:08:09.388 --> 00:08:14.260
but he felt he couldn't
sacrifice the comedy inherent

00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:16.128
in the words reptile house.

00:08:19.465 --> 00:08:22.901
[ Laughter ]
It's always a little
disappointing that it's not --

00:08:22.901 --> 00:08:25.004
It feels like monkey --
Is it monkeys and reptiles

00:08:25.004 --> 00:08:28.074
are the only ones in the zoo
who get houses?

00:08:28.074 --> 00:08:29.975
Right?

00:08:29.975 --> 00:08:31.043
Here's what I'm saying.

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:33.145
You want people
to come to your zoo?

00:08:33.145 --> 00:08:34.680
Make it look like a tiny house.

00:08:36.281 --> 00:08:38.016
Don't make it just look like
another part of the zoo

00:08:38.016 --> 00:08:39.851
that's got a roof on it.

00:08:39.851 --> 00:08:41.487
Make it look like
a suburban home

00:08:41.487 --> 00:08:45.057
and just let the reptiles run.

00:08:45.057 --> 00:08:47.025
[ Laughter ]

00:08:47.025 --> 00:08:49.028
Or maybe you hate having people
come to your zoo.

00:08:50.996 --> 00:08:52.664
Speaking of animals,

00:08:52.664 --> 00:08:55.634
we had a joke about

00:08:55.634 --> 00:08:58.203
kids playing with a bobcat

00:08:58.203 --> 00:09:00.172
and we played audio.

00:09:00.172 --> 00:09:04.110
Very surprising --
more than one of you said,

00:09:04.110 --> 00:09:06.679
"That's not a bobcat.
That's a mountain lion."

00:09:06.679 --> 00:09:10.549
And you got us dead to rights.

00:09:10.549 --> 00:09:11.683
We went.
We reached out.

00:09:11.683 --> 00:09:14.153
We tried to cast a bobcat.

00:09:14.153 --> 00:09:15.421
[ Laughter ]

00:09:15.421 --> 00:09:17.456
We work with one of the best
animal talent agents

00:09:17.456 --> 00:09:18.790
in New York City.

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:22.060
And it was not -- The best we
could do is we got --

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:23.829
this is the mountain lion
we got...

00:09:25.664 --> 00:09:28.034 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
And --

00:09:31.437 --> 00:09:34.106 line:0%
And so, [indistinct] Reggie

00:09:34.106 --> 00:09:35.374
and, if you can see, though,

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:36.776
the reason we --

00:09:36.776 --> 00:09:38.076
I don't know if we'll be able
to pop in on this,

00:09:38.076 --> 00:09:40.979
but we have his

00:09:40.979 --> 00:09:43.949
acting résumé right here.

00:09:43.949 --> 00:09:45.985
But it says that,
special skills and interests,

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:50.456
he did say,
"Great at improv. Some guitar.

00:09:50.456 --> 00:09:53.325
[ Laughter ]
Chasing down and killing prey.

00:09:53.325 --> 00:09:56.762
Good with dialects --
French, Bobcat,

00:09:56.762 --> 00:10:00.099
[ Laughter ]
and Borat voice.

00:10:00.099 --> 00:10:01.767
[ Laughter ]

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:02.668
So.

00:10:06.505 --> 00:10:07.940
Ol' Reggie Cantrell.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:09.075
Supposedly good to work with.

00:10:10.176 --> 00:10:12.278
[ Laughter ]

00:10:12.278 --> 00:10:13.779
Because we get him in the booth.

00:10:16.248 --> 00:10:17.482
I guess they say
the hardest part is

00:10:17.482 --> 00:10:18.784
getting the headphones on.

00:10:18.784 --> 00:10:20.319
[ Laughter ]
Because they're not used

00:10:20.319 --> 00:10:21.787
to hearing their own voice.

00:10:21.787 --> 00:10:24.557
[ Laughter ]

00:10:26.858 --> 00:10:29.628
But I called up the audio guy
today and I was like,

00:10:29.628 --> 00:10:31.930
"How was -- How is Reggie?"

00:10:31.930 --> 00:10:32.932
And he's in the hospital.

00:10:32.932 --> 00:10:35.635
[ Laughter ]

00:10:38.403 --> 00:10:41.173
Talked about having one --

00:10:41.173 --> 00:10:43.341
like the lifeguard
had one Wordle guess left

00:10:43.341 --> 00:10:45.143
and then we put this up
and everybody's like,

00:10:45.143 --> 00:10:46.344
"That's not his last guess

00:10:46.344 --> 00:10:48.413
and also, the letters above
aren't right

00:10:48.413 --> 00:10:51.116
and this is bad Wordle.
[ Mumbles ]" So, anyway.

00:10:51.116 --> 00:10:53.251
[ Laughter ]
Pbbbt!

00:10:53.251 --> 00:10:56.354
So I went down to graphics
and I'm like, "Guys!

00:10:56.354 --> 00:10:58.123
What's up?
Do you not play Wordle?"

00:10:58.123 --> 00:10:59.792
And they were like, "No."

00:10:59.792 --> 00:11:01.627
I was like, "Why not?"
And they're like,

00:11:01.627 --> 00:11:04.262
"Everyone who plays it
is an insufferable dork."

00:11:04.262 --> 00:11:06.665
[ Laughter ]
And I was like, "I play it."

00:11:06.665 --> 00:11:11.270
And then -- Again, I don't like
to be the guy who does this.

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:12.738
They work for me.

00:11:12.738 --> 00:11:15.574
[ Laughter ]
And I said, "Hey! I play it."

00:11:15.574 --> 00:11:17.009
And they just went like this.
They went,

00:11:17.009 --> 00:11:19.044
"Oh, we know."

00:11:19.044 --> 00:11:22.080
[ Laughter ]
And then close the door so slow.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.915
They were like --

00:11:23.915 --> 00:11:26.652
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:35.127
Everybody was upset that Samberg
was not in the "Specjackular."

00:11:35.127 --> 00:11:36.128
Here's the thing.

00:11:36.128 --> 00:11:37.896
I don't know if he's going
to answer

00:11:37.896 --> 00:11:39.732
and I wanted
the "Specjackular" --

00:11:39.732 --> 00:11:42.735
I wanted a semblance of control
and I feel like

00:11:42.735 --> 00:11:44.703
it's ha ha funny
when he doesn't answer,

00:11:44.703 --> 00:11:45.837
when we're doing
a "Corrections,"

00:11:45.837 --> 00:11:47.605
but a "Corrections"
is not a "Specjackular."

00:11:47.605 --> 00:11:50.008
We've established they're two
very different things.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:54.713
And like for big moments,
you don't want to risk

00:11:54.713 --> 00:11:58.350
the person not being there,
you know?

00:11:58.350 --> 00:12:00.819
If they called up
to Neil Armstrong

00:12:00.819 --> 00:12:01.987
after the moon landing,
they're like --

00:12:01.987 --> 00:12:02.721
[ Transatlantic accent ]
We've got the president,

00:12:02.721 --> 00:12:03.889
would like to say hello.

00:12:03.889 --> 00:12:05.123
And they're like,
"Oh, well, we'd love to talk

00:12:05.123 --> 00:12:06.392
to the president,"
and then you just heard like

00:12:06.392 --> 00:12:07.793
[ As line ringing ]
pbbbrrrp.

00:12:07.793 --> 00:12:09.161
[ Laughter ]

00:12:09.161 --> 00:12:10.262
Pbbbrrrp.

00:12:10.262 --> 00:12:12.398
[ Laughter ]

00:12:12.398 --> 00:12:13.399
Pbbbrrrp.

00:12:13.399 --> 00:12:15.568
[ Laughter ]

00:12:15.568 --> 00:12:16.569
Pbbbrrrp.

00:12:18.904 --> 00:12:19.671
Pbbbrrrp.
[ Laughter ]

00:12:19.671 --> 00:12:20.905
"We're real sorry, Neil.

00:12:20.905 --> 00:12:22.474
I don't think he's here."

00:12:22.474 --> 00:12:24.243
[ Laughter ]

00:12:24.243 --> 00:12:26.912
Um...

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:28.047
We'll try him today, though.

00:12:32.284 --> 00:12:34.019
Been a while
since I've called him.

00:12:35.887 --> 00:12:37.089
[ Ring ]

00:12:39.024 --> 00:12:40.993
[ Ring ]
He probably doesn't even know

00:12:40.993 --> 00:12:42.895
there was a "Specjackular."
[ Ring ]

00:12:42.895 --> 00:12:44.763
Or how many episodes
we've even done.

00:12:44.763 --> 00:12:46.231
[ Ring ]
He's not going to answer.

00:12:46.231 --> 00:12:48.033
See? This is it.
Do you guys like this?

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:49.534
[ Ring ]
You're like,
"Why wasn't Andy there?"

00:12:49.534 --> 00:12:50.969
Because he's a bad friend.

00:12:50.969 --> 00:12:52.571
[ Ring ]
[ Laughter ]

00:12:54.072 --> 00:12:55.407
[ Ring ]
Alright.

00:12:55.407 --> 00:12:56.241
I'll leave the ringer on.

00:12:56.241 --> 00:12:57.710
He's not a bad friend.

00:12:57.710 --> 00:12:59.744
Okay.

00:12:59.744 --> 00:13:04.783
I said that Paul Revere said,
"The British are coming."

00:13:04.783 --> 00:13:06.384
He did not say that.
At the time,

00:13:06.384 --> 00:13:08.287
everybody considered
themselves British.

00:13:08.287 --> 00:13:10.990
That would not have been
a helpful thing to say.

00:13:10.990 --> 00:13:12.458
That would've been like
the dogs asking,

00:13:12.458 --> 00:13:13.892
"Who let the dogs out?"

00:13:13.892 --> 00:13:17.096
[ Laughter ]

00:13:17.096 --> 00:13:20.266
But he probably said,
"The regulars are coming,"

00:13:20.266 --> 00:13:21.900
which is --

00:13:21.900 --> 00:13:23.035
The regulars are coming.

00:13:23.035 --> 00:13:24.370
"The regulars are coming!
The regulars!"

00:13:24.370 --> 00:13:26.872
That's awful,
but I guess that's what he said.

00:13:26.872 --> 00:13:32.110
Also, I mentioned the poem
by Henry Wadsworth Longfellow

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:34.446
and a couple of you said,
"It's Wordsworth."

00:13:34.446 --> 00:13:36.482
It's not Wordsworth.
It's Wadsworth.

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.518
There was Williams Wordsworth.

00:13:39.518 --> 00:13:43.288
William Wordsworth
was a poet, first,

00:13:43.288 --> 00:13:46.124
and then there was Henry --
It was Wordsworth.

00:13:46.124 --> 00:13:47.993
It was
Henry Wordsworth Longfellow,

00:13:47.993 --> 00:13:49.728
but in the poetry union,

00:13:49.728 --> 00:13:51.397
like you can't have
the same name.

00:13:51.397 --> 00:13:53.065
[ Laughter ]

00:13:53.065 --> 00:13:55.834
It's like a guild.

00:13:55.834 --> 00:13:58.770
They went to him like,
"We already have a Wordsworth.

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:00.005
You got to come up
with something best."

00:14:00.005 --> 00:14:01.473
And, because he was a poet

00:14:01.473 --> 00:14:02.707
and he had a way with language,

00:14:02.707 --> 00:14:04.476
he said, "Wadsworth."

00:14:04.476 --> 00:14:05.678
[ Laughter ]

00:14:09.615 --> 00:14:11.750
So, we joked about the fact

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.653
that the reason Paul Revere
is the famous one,

00:14:14.653 --> 00:14:17.088
instead of Prescott
or William Dawes,

00:14:17.088 --> 00:14:18.957
the other two riders,
is that his name

00:14:18.957 --> 00:14:21.560
had a better rhyme scheme,
you know?

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:23.661
Revere is --
you got that "ear" sound.

00:14:23.661 --> 00:14:25.130
Lot of words in there.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.531
So,

00:14:26.531 --> 00:14:30.101
turns out, I'm not the first
person to make this observation.

00:14:30.101 --> 00:14:34.239
Turns out, in 1896,

00:14:34.239 --> 00:14:39.778
a woman named Helen F. Moore
wrote a poem called

00:14:39.778 --> 00:14:42.781
"The Midnight Ride
of William Dawes,"

00:14:42.781 --> 00:14:48.554
which was 100 years
after our friend Longfellow,

00:14:48.554 --> 00:14:51.690
and it begins,
"I am a wandering, bitter shade,

00:14:51.690 --> 00:14:53.325
Never of me was a hero made;

00:14:53.325 --> 00:14:55.460
Poets have never sung my praise,

00:14:55.460 --> 00:14:58.497
Nobody crowned
my brow with bays;

00:14:58.497 --> 00:15:00.699
And if you ask me
the fatal cause,

00:15:00.699 --> 00:15:03.602
I answer only,
"My name was Dawes."

00:15:05.204 --> 00:15:07.072
It finishes --
"History rings with" the --

00:15:07.072 --> 00:15:09.808
"History rings
with his silvery name;

00:15:09.808 --> 00:15:11.810
Closed to me are
the portals of fame.

00:15:11.810 --> 00:15:15.014
Had he been Dawes and I Revere,

00:15:15.014 --> 00:15:17.015
No one had heard of him, I fear.

00:15:17.015 --> 00:15:18.483
No one has heard of me because

00:15:18.483 --> 00:15:21.319
He was Revere and I was Dawes."

00:15:21.319 --> 00:15:24.256
That is "The Midnight Ride
of William Dawes,"

00:15:24.256 --> 00:15:25.557
by Helen F. Moore,

00:15:25.557 --> 00:15:29.294
of whom very little is known
about Helen F. Moore.

00:15:29.294 --> 00:15:32.897
But scholars believe
the F stands for

00:15:32.897 --> 00:15:34.299
"[bleep] Paul Revere."

00:15:34.299 --> 00:15:37.269
[ Laughter ]

00:15:40.873 --> 00:15:41.840
Um -- Sorry.

00:15:43.008 --> 00:15:45.677 line:0%
If anybody's -- he is open,
if anybody's casting.

00:15:45.677 --> 00:15:49.014 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:15:49.014 --> 00:15:53.419
You guys, this is --
We're off and running, they say.

00:15:53.419 --> 00:15:54.953
And --

00:15:54.953 --> 00:15:59.791
Oh, we're about to
take a two-week hiatus

00:15:59.791 --> 00:16:05.364
and that means see me
in three weeks.

